hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15822","SOURCE TRUNCATED: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us: Hajjaj, meaning al-Sawwaf, narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ikrimah, from al-Hajjaj ibn Amr al-Ansari, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say:"
"15823","And Ismail said: al-Hajjaj ibn Abi Uthman informed me, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us that Ikrimah, the freed slave of Ibn Abbas, narrated to him, he said: al-Hajjaj ibn Amr al-Ansari narrated to me, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever breaks a bone or becomes lame has become released from ihram, but another Hajj is due upon him. He said: So I mentioned that to Ibn Abbas and Abu Hurayrah, and they both said: He spoke the truth. Ismail said: So I narrated that to Ibn Abbas and Abu Hurayrah, and they both said: He spoke the truth."
